--- !u!114 &565193707
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 565193706}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 5edf6b9814176a54d84e97b6a2a688de, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Skygrind.Game::Skygrind.Game.MapAuthoring.MapRoot
  mapId: drydock
  why: 'DRYDOCK (NIGHT15 U3-28.6; MAP-DESIGN.md sections 3.1 and 4): "Finish the
    ship, or fight on its bones." A sky-shipyard cut into a cliff at dusk, the last
    airship half-built in its cradle. The hub, THE CRADLE, is THE RING: a 172 m training
    loop around the unfinished hull and its 64 m mast (the landmark, seen from every
    zone), cut in two by the keel corridor, with aimed pads up to the hull deck;
    each side zone is built for its verbs (THE RIBS: a canyon of 8-12 m slabs 7 m
    apart to wall-ride and wall-jump; THE SLIPWAY: two 40 m launch ramps down from
    a 10 m deck and a pad back up), and THE GANGWAY is the start, the mast in view
    through its door. Tonight''s greybox builds these four zones; the boilerworks,
    the drafting office, the gantry and the pier are night 2. New design, so Unity-side
    (CLAUDE.md rule 5: the web never had this map); every number comes from Design/maps/drydock.plan.json,
    sized from the movement numbers in MAP-DESIGN.md section 1, and Assets/Editor/Maps/Build_drydock.cs
    turns it into this file. The map''s identity is GG''s decision (D-59): this is
    the recommended concept, built to be played and judged.'
  floorSize: 128
  killPlaneY: -30
  startZone: gangway
  hasCore: 1
  core:
    x0: 0
    z0: 0
    cells: 0
    cellSize: 4
  importedFrom: Design/maps/drydock.json
  extraDataJson: 
